      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791537911063,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NOTES\n\n- Blocks per direction = matrix size / block size, rounded UP:\nblocks_x = wdith.div_ceil(4)\nblocks_y = height.div_ceil(4)\n\n- 64 threads for 25 elements = 39 idle.\n\n- Edge blocks hang over the right and bottom sides.\n\n- Bounds check, two parts: \ncol < width (right edge)\nrow < height (bottom edge)\n\n- Check BEFORE linearizing: a too-big col wraps into the next row\ne.g. (row 0, col 6) -> 0 * 5 + 6 = 6\n= (row 1, col 1), someone else's element\n\n- Same idea as Stage 0's 24 idle threads, now in 2 directions.\n\n- 4 x 4 blocks are just for the drawing. In the code we use\n16 x 16 = 256 threads (a multiple of 32).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NOTES\n\n- Blocks per direction = matrix size / block size, rounded UP:\nblocks_x = wdith.div_ceil(4)\nblocks_y = height.div_ceil(4)\n\n- 64 threads for 25 elements = 39 idle.\n\n- Edge blocks hang over the right and bottom sides.\n\n- Bounds check, two parts: \ncol < width (right edge)\nrow < height (bottom edge)\n\n- Check BEFORE linearizing: a too-big col wraps into the next row\ne.g. (row 0, col 6) -> 0 * 5 + 6 = 6\n= (row 1, col 1), someone else's element\n\n- Same idea as Stage 0's 24 idle threads, now in 2 directions.\n\n- 4 x 4 blocks are just for the drawing. In the code we use\n16 x 16 = 256 threads (a multiple of 32).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
